    "explanation": "Let dp[i] say whether the prefix of length i can be segmented, with dp[0] = true. The prefix works if some earlier position j is reachable and s[j:i] is a dictionary word. Putting the words in a set and only looking back at most max word length makes this O(n * L) set lookups. Unmemoised recursion is exponential on strings like 'aaa...ab'.",
    "code": "class Solution:\n    def wordBreak(self, s: str, wordDict: List[str]) -> bool:\n        words = set(wordDict)\n        longest = max(len(w) for w in words)\n        dp = [True] + [False] * len(s)\n        for i in range(1, len(s) + 1):\n            for j in range(max(0, i - longest), i):\n                if dp[j] and s[j:i] in words:\n                    dp[i] = True\n                    break\n        return dp[-1]\n"
